  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "William Jaird Levitt was an American property developer whose Levittown communities helped shape postwar suburbia. As president of Levitt & Sons, he applied mass production to housing, making homeownership accessible to thousands of returning servicemen and their families. His developments also enforced racial restrictions that excluded Black buyers from those opportunities.",
